From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1061 redfin: AppleBasebandPCI stand-in, /dev/abpbridge, ABM
 fake boot in CommCenter (sweetabp, default off)

Boot-arg sweetabp (bitmask, default 0: nothing changes): 1 publishes stand-ins
for Apple's baseband drivers (a "baseband" nub with the D22AP config,
AppleBaseband, AppleBasebandPCIControl with bootstage, AppleBasebandPCIInterface
qmux1/qmux2 with the AppleBasebandPCI user-client ABI: open/close/write/read
sync+async/start/abort) and /dev/abpbridge, which hands every frame CommCenter
writes to wland and completes CommCenter's reads with wland's frames. 2 (or
sweetabmfake=1): in a process named CommCenter, shared_region_check_np()
verifies the 10 instructions of capabilities::bb::abm::shouldBoot() in the
shared cache and makes that one page a private copy-on-write copy where it
returns 0 (cs_allow_invalid + VM_PROT_COPY, as a debugger does), so ABM takes
its "Faking bootup" path. Sysctls kern.sweet_abp (add bits at run time),
kern.sweet_abp_bootstage, kern.sweet_abp_msg, kern.sweet_abp_stats.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013SvAC32FNcvdmiSrHtBxEq
